.nh
.TH "PB-TEAM-GET" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-team-get - Show one team and its current generation


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb team get <team> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Show one team and its current generation

.PP
Read one team's current membership, permissions, and generation. Use the returned generation for the next mutation to avoid overwriting a newer change.

.PP
Teams use explicit membership and resource grants. Membership alone does not grant machine use, ENV values, previews, or tunnels. Mutations use the current team generation to reject stale edits; read pb team get before retrying a conflicting change.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for get

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-team(1)\fP
